# Key Takeaways

* LLM stands for Large Language Model.
* An LLM takes user input and generates a response.
* User input is called input tokens.
* Model output is called output tokens.
* GPT stands for Generative Pre-trained Transformer.
* Generative means the model creates output.
* Pre-trained means the model has already learned from large datasets.
* Transformer refers to the model architecture.
* Search engines mainly search and return links.
* LLMs generate natural language responses.
* GPT is a very descriptive name because it directly explains the type of model.
* The next important concept is the Transformer architecture.
